  "implementation": [
    "Move-only JobMemory from original PreparedMemory::Borrow passively offers exact controller-owned backing to one distinct actual same-Domain NativeThreads sibling. Pinned unique shared JobState nodes avoid reused-index/ABA identity; bound64 unreaped nodes is selected HOST policy.",
    "Acquire atomically reserves Offered->Acquiring, verifies distinct actual FLS/PTD/NativeThreads marker and retains actual self-thread duplicate outside mutex. Adopt handle before postcheck; known duplicate failure restores Offered, unknown admission retains poison/handle.",
    "Acquired memory validates exact child thread/fiber/PTD/root. Return invalidates token but may transfer a live allocation to original source owner. Main Borrow refuses logical return while any child offer/acquire/borrow is pending or backing allocation/poison remains.",
    "Original worker reap_jobs polls only returned child handles with zero timeout, and closes/recycles only after actual OS/FLS exit. Timeout retains; failed/unknown outcome poisons. Per-call reservation, root/exact-handle postchecks and null committed closed prefixes prevent replay.",
    "Controller close waits original and every admitted child exit before releasing backing, with one shared finite wait budget across all handles. Default one-worker path remains and no Parent/Profile/Graph affinity is removed.",
    "New source tests describe capacity/cancel/reuse, move/controller/original/foreign/double-acquire rejection, two exited-child recycling rounds, live allocation transfer, logical versus physical exit and isolated abandoned-job retention. None compiled/run."
  ],
